#: 2036730c0f754e249da552fd9a33b684
msgid ""
"Search inside of the ``qubes.xml`` file for the ``backup-path`` of the qube "
"whose data you wish to restore. If you install the ``xmlstarlet`` package, "
"the following command will convert ``qubes.xml`` to a friendlier listing for "
"this purpose:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:183
#: bd743d68e2554fd9914a57934044e64e
msgid ""
"The example output above shows that the backup file includes a qube named "
"``personal`` and a qube named ``vault``, with ``backup-path`` values of "
"``vm123/`` and ``vm321/`` respectively. (Every other listed qube was not "
"selected to be included in the backup file.) Use the corresponding value to "
"untar the necessary data files of the qube:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:191
#: ea2966b825164648b26e16e55555fef0
msgid "Verify and decrypt the backed up data, decompress it, and extract it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:202
#: 4e15bbf77ee844a987a03248a8a8320f
msgid ""
"If this pipeline fails, it is likely that the backup is corrupted or has "
"been tampered with. Also see the note in step 6 about substituting a "
"different compression program for ``gzip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:205
#: 9a6f6a4db9ea4012ad65ad5616c6ebb5
msgid "Mount ``private.img`` and access your data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/backup-emergency-restore-v4.rst:207
#: 1b227ae9416044bdac6775cb846862ee
msgid ""
"Beside the security risk of accessing compromised *files*,  there can be "
"security consequences of simply mounting *file systems* if an attacker had "
"been able to compromise the file system in some way. For better security, "
"handle these files within an isolated environment like a dedicated VM, a "
"Live USB, or by using `libguestfs <https://libguestfs.org/>`__"
msgstr ""

